  "verbalization": "Vidalol B is implicated in the interaction with HPAC through a series of molecular pathways, with SNU-387 acting as a central mediator. The evidence suggests that Vidalol B targets SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, Tetraethylammonium, and 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, dl-. These compounds all ultimately have HPAC as their target. The varying scores in the paths indicate a consistent but not absolute relationship, likely due to the complexity of the biological network and the multiple layers of interaction. The presence of multiple targets at SNU-387 suggests a potential mechanism where Vidalol B may modulate the activity of this compound, which then influences HPAC. This integrated pathway highlights the importance of SNU-387 in linking Vidalol B to HPAC, emphasizing the role of this intermediary in the drug's mechanism of action.",
